From f3ed5c30e37eb3467050a63402b4a1b8353af6f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GabbeHags <gabbehags@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 22:36:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 21/24] perf(shader): keep specialized SPIR-V in the shader
 disk cache

Every run re-specialized each first-seen shader on the queue worker:
specializeModule memoizes only in-process, keyed on the per-run variant
id. In one title's city load that is ~560 shaders at ~4.8 ms each.

Specialized modules are now ordinary shader disk cache entries
(LoadSpecialized / StoreSpecialized): the wrapEntry header holds the
full key, so a different key never loads an entry and truncated or
corrupt files are rejected, and the cache's writer thread writes them
instead of the queue worker. The key is the artifact's SPIR-V content
hash, vertex classes, specialization constants and the SpirvTarget
fields, laid out field by field, followed by the recompiler switch key
as for the other entries; it also covers target.nonConstantImageOffsets
and takes the feature digest through the same unsealed fallback as
RecompileCacheKey. The cache is on whenever the shader disk cache is;
APS5_NO_SPECIALIZED_CACHE=1 (a neutral switch) turns it off, and
[shader-disk-cache] counts the entries as specialized modules.

agc_shader_disk_cache_tests gains verifySpecializedStore and
verifySpecializedSwitch; USAGE.md and ENVIRONMENT.md document the cache
and the switch.

That title's city load, warm caches, same build, APS5_TRACE_SECONDS=35:20,
RTX 2070 SUPER: 567 specialized hits; slowest frame 2328.5 ms with
APS5_NO_SPECIALIZED_CACHE=1, 1639.2 ms with the cache.

From boykopovar/AnyPS5#26800 (open; 4e9f3ab7ed and ac8c6e5678 squashed),
on top of the failure memo: its jobs and counters sit beside the
recorded compile failures.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
